<h1>1. Project Overview</h1>
<p><strong>PaperBull</strong> is a modern, real-time paper-trading (simulated stock trading) platform and market intelligence dashboard built specifically for the Indian Equity Market (NSE/BSE). It grants users a virtual wallet of <strong>₹1,00,000.00</strong> to trade over 2,000+ Indian equities, test intraday (MIS) and delivery (CNC) trading strategies, analyze real-time technical sparklines, inspect company fundamentals, track IPO Grey Market Premiums (GMP), and chat with an embedded Google Gemini AI financial assistant.</p>

<h3>What Problem Does It Solve?</h3>
<p>Retail investors and aspiring traders in India face significant barriers when learning stock market trading:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Financial Risk</strong>: Real money trading without prior strategy validation leads to rapid capital depletion.</li>
  <li><strong>Delayed & Fragmented Information</strong>: Most free tools provide static 15-minute delayed data or lack sector-wide screening, financial income statements, and market depth visualization in one workspace.</li>
  <li><strong>Complex Intraday Square-Off Rules</strong>: Real stockbrokers automatically liquidate intraday (MIS) positions before the market close (3:15 PM IST). Novice traders often misunderstand this margin rule. PaperBull models exact EOD intraday square-offs server-side.</li>
</ul>

<h3>How Does the Complete System Work?</h3>
<p>PaperBull operates as a <strong>Decoupled Three-Tier Microservice Architecture</strong>:</p>
<ul>
  <li><strong>Client Tier (<code>/frontend</code>)</strong>: Single-page application modules (HTML5, Vanilla CSS, React via CDN, and Vanilla JS) running in the browser.</li>
  <li><strong>Market Data & AI Microservice (<code>/nse-node</code>, Port 5000)</strong>: Node.js/Express service that interfaces with Yahoo Finance APIs, parses official NSE CSV master lists, caches 2,000+ stock quotes, and orchestrates autonomous Google Gemini AI agents for live market news and IPO tracking.</li>
  <li><strong>Trading Engine & Auth Microservice (<code>/paperbull-node</code>, Port 8000)</strong>: Node.js/Express service backed by PostgreSQL. Manages user registration, Bcrypt hashing, Google OAuth 2.0 via Passport, atomic portfolio ledger transactions, weighted average buy price updates, realized P&L bookkeeping, and an automated background intraday square-off cron job.</li>
</ul>

